From 9df5c0a4fe335af88f4464c2e6316ac26a041c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: GP100 (sm_60) fp16 matrix-vector path for batch 1..8

sm_60 has no __dp4a, so MMVQ emulated every int8 dot and ran at 40-49% of HBM2 bandwidth. New
mmvq-gp100.cu: activations converted once to fp16 (power-of-two prescale per 32-block, exact fp32 block
sums), weights unpacked by PRMT straight into subnormal half bit patterns (q*2^-24, exact; HFMA2 is full
rate on subnormals), HFMA2 accumulation within a sub-block, fp32 flush. Q3_K/Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/IQ4_XS/IQ4_NL/
Q8_0 single-column, fused gate/up/SWIGLU, 2..8 columns for Q4_K/Q5_K/IQ4_XS (speculative verification),
activation-conversion cache per graph evaluation, fused single-row RMS_NORM*weight that fills that cache.
Device code is sm_60-only.

Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, 2x P100, -sm tensor: tg128 25.04 -> 33.22, pp512 unchanged; MTP (draft 3) on a
real-use prompt set 26.15 -> 40.91 tok/s. Decode-path KLD vs a Q8_0 reference 0.011857 -> 0.011263 (-ub 1),
0.011880 -> 0.011456 (-ub 5). test-backend-ops MUL_MAT/MUL_MAT_ID/MUL_MAT_VEC_FUSION/GLU/RMS_NORM pass.

